Subject: [H0 g0q] Correct the reachable HS-PHY REFCLK mask/value order

The helper takes mask, value. Select the intended two-bit value without
preserving an unknown low bit. The normal FYG8 vendor consumer uses mask 3,
value 2. The same correction appears in Qualcomm's 2026-10-06 v5 4/6 patch:
https://lkml.iu.edu/2610.0/09839.html

Only the fixed-peripheral init path is changed. The unrelated host-only
AUTO_RESUME hunk is outside this candidate. This patch proves no device cause.

--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-snps-femto-v2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-snps-femto-v2.c
@@ -429,7 +429,7 @@ static int qcom_snps_hsphy_init(struct phy *phy)
 					USB2_PHY_USB_PHY_HS_PHY_CTRL_COMMON1,
 					PLLBTUNE, PLLBTUNE);
 	qcom_snps_hsphy_write_mask(hsphy->base, USB2_PHY_USB_PHY_REFCLK_CTRL,
-					REFCLK_SEL_DEFAULT, REFCLK_SEL_MASK);
+					REFCLK_SEL_MASK, REFCLK_SEL_DEFAULT);
 	qcom_snps_hsphy_write_mask(hsphy->base,
 					USB2_PHY_USB_PHY_HS_PHY_CTRL_COMMON1,
 					VBUSVLDEXTSEL0, VBUSVLDEXTSEL0);
